{
  "_comment": [
    "Cross-language canonical-byte vectors for the v4 signed pairing invite.",
    "The Rust host signs; the Kotlin client verifies. If the two canonical",
    "encodings diverge by one character, EVERY signature fails to verify - and",
    "it fails silently, on a phone, with both sides compiling and both sides'",
    "own tests green. This file is what catches that in CI instead.",
    "",
    "Both directions are recorded on purpose. `rust_generated` is verified by",
    "Kotlin; `kotlin_generated` is verified by Rust. One side alone would only",
    "prove that side is self-consistent.",
    "",
    "Regenerate deliberately, never by hand:",
    "  cargo run -p pairing --example generate_vector",
    "  (cd apk && ./gradlew :app:testDebugUnitTest --tests '*InviteV4Test*')",
    "then read KOTLIN_VECTOR lines out of the test XML system-out.",
    "",
    "Field order in canonical_utf8 is LOAD-BEARING and is not alphabetical."
  ],
